### 3.2 — Build the interactive map

Build the Leaflet map with the following requirements:

- At least **two distinct data layers** (one social, one environmental)
- A **layer toggle control** (`addLayersControl()` with `overlayGroups`) that lets the user turn each layer on or off independently
- At least **one additional interactive feature** of your choosing that is meaningful for YOUR specific map. Options include (but are not limited to):
  - Popups with attribute data
  - Hover labels
  - A minimap (`addMiniMap()` from `leaflet.extras`)
  - Marker clustering
  - A scale bar (`addScaleBar()`)
  - Highlighting on hover (`highlight` argument in `addPolygons()`)
- A legend for at least one layer

Document your "one thing" choice in a comment explaining what it is and why it fits your map.

```{r task3_map, echo=TRUE, message=TRUE}
# your code here
# population density
pal_density <- colorBin(
  palette = "Purples",
  domain = sa2$pop_density,
  bins = 5
)

# park types
pal_parks <- colorFactor(
  palette = c("yellow", "green", "darkgreen", "orange"),
  levels = unique(parks_all$park_type))

leaflet() %>%
  setView(lng = -84.4, lat = 39.2, zoom = 7) %>%
  addProviderTiles(providers$CartoDB.Positron) %>%
  # population density
  addPolygons(
    data = sa2,
    fillColor = ~pal_density(pop_density),
    color = "black",
    weight = 1,
    fillOpacity = 0.7,
    group = "Population Density",
    popup = ~paste0(
      "<b>County:</b> ", NAME, "<br>",
      "<b>Population Density:</b> ", round(pop_density, 2))) %>%
  # parks
  addPolygons(
    data = parks_all,
    fillColor = ~pal_parks(park_type),
    color = "darkgreen",
    weight = 1,
    fillOpacity = 0.6,
    group = "Parks",
    popup = ~paste0("<b>Park Type:</b> ", park_type)) %>%
  # layer control
  addLayersControl(
    overlayGroups = c("Population Density", "Parks"),
    options = layersControlOptions(collapsed = FALSE)) %>%
  # legend for pop
  addLegend(
    pal = pal_density,
    values = sa2$pop_density,
    title = "Population Density",
    position = "bottomright") %>%
  # legend for parks
  addLegend(
    pal = pal_parks,
    values = parks_all$park_type,
    title = "Park Type",
    position = "bottomleft") %>%
  # my one extrathing
  addScaleBar()
